.IX Title "LEI-DAEMON-KILL 1"
.TH LEI-DAEMON-KILL 1 1993-10-02 public-inbox.git "public-inbox user manual"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "نام (NAME)"
lei\-daemon\-kill \- signal the lei\-daemon
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
lei daemon\-kill [\-SIGNAL | \-s SIGNAL | \-\-signal SIGNAL]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Send a signal to the \fBlei\-daemon\fR\|(8).  \f(CW\*(C`SIGNAL\*(C'\fR defaults to \f(CW\*(C`TERM\*(C'\fR.
.PP
This command should be run after updating the code of lei.
.SH SIGNALS
.IX Header "SIGNALS"
.IP SIGTERM 8
.IX Item "SIGTERM"
Send a graceful termination signal.  \fBlei\-daemon\fR\|(8) will exit
when all currently running lei commands are done.  The listen
socket will be released as soon as the signal is processed
so another \fBlei\-daemon\fR\|(8) process can take its place.
.IP SIGKILL 8
.IX Item "SIGKILL"
Kills \fBlei\-daemon\fR\|(8) immediately.  Some worker processes may
remain running for a short while.
.SH CONTACT
.IX Header "CONTACT"
